From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: serlk <22211586+Serlk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 21:00:22 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 35/35] arm64: dts: mediatek: mt6878-unihertz-titan2: Enable
 the ISP RAW path on -all

Move the image signal processor path of the -raw test board into the
camera description included by -all (mt6878-unihertz-titan2-cameras.dtsi):

- larbs 16/17 (RAW-A/YUV-A) and 33/34 (RAW-B/YUV-B),
- the RAW-A, YUV-A, RAW-B and YUV-B engines, RAW-B as the second engine
  of RAW-A (mediatek,twin),
- the second destination of CSI port 2 (IMX766): endpoint@1 of seninf
  port@5 toward RAW-A, next to the camsv1 endpoint, which stays.

The engines take their power domain and clocks by runtime PM only while
the RAW video node streams; the YUV engines and the larbs follow through
device links, so nothing of the path is on at idle.

-raw is now the same as -all and stays for the boot scripts. The new
-all DTB is byte-identical to the previous -raw DTB. The boards built on
-all (-all-iommu, -all-ovl34, -charger-diag, -charger-test, -jpeg,
-sleep, -sleep-disp, -sleep-disp-iommu, -vcp, -vcp-iommu) follow; the
other boards are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../mediatek/mt6878-unihertz-titan2-all.dts   |  3 +-
 .../mt6878-unihertz-titan2-cameras.dtsi       | 75 ++++++++++++++++++-
 .../mediatek/mt6878-unihertz-titan2-raw.dts   | 67 ++---------------
 3 files changed, 80 insertions(+), 65 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6878-unihertz-titan2-all.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6878-unihertz-titan2-all.dts
index 6da4fa48830a..501e50dc5ec6 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6878-unihertz-titan2-all.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6878-unihertz-titan2-all.dts
@@ -4,7 +4,8 @@
  * Same as -all-fb plus the -drm stage, plus the MT6375 charger with the
  * Type-C port manager (PD sink 5 V / 9 V, host role with VBUS from the
  * charger's OTG boost) and USB in OTG mode, plus the three cameras on their
- * CAMSV engines behind the multimedia IOMMU
+ * CAMSV engines behind the multimedia IOMMU and the main camera also
+ * through the RAW and YUV engines of the image signal processor
  * (mt6878-unihertz-titan2-cameras.dtsi), with the factory device tree
  * battery limits (2.05 A, CV 4.45 V).
  *
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6878-unihertz-titan2-cameras.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6878-unihertz-titan2-cameras.dtsi
index 4ecec599b3a8..1e5839c0e8c8 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6878-unihertz-titan2-cameras.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6878-unihertz-titan2-cameras.dtsi
@@ -1,7 +1,9 @@
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0-only OR MIT)
 /*
  * Unihertz Titan 2: the three cameras, each on its own CAMSV engine behind
- * the MM IOMMU, so user space (libcamera) sees three cameras at once.
+ * the MM IOMMU, so user space (libcamera) sees three cameras at once, and
+ * the main camera (IMX766) also through the RAW and YUV engines of the
+ * image signal processor (see "ISP path" below).
  * Included by mt6878-unihertz-titan2-all.dts.
  *
  *   sensor    bus        CSI port  seninf  mux  cam mux  CAMSV (camsv-id)  larb
@@ -35,7 +37,9 @@
  * regulator core. Reset and power down lines are the sensor drivers' GPIOs.
  *
  * Paths to memory: camsv1 larb14 -> cam sub-common 1; camsv2 larb13 and
- * camsv5 larb29 -> cam sub-common 0; both sub-commons -> cam-vcore
+ * camsv5 larb29 -> cam sub-common 0; RAW-A larb16 and YUV-B larb34 -> cam
+ * sub-common 0, YUV-A larb17 and RAW-B larb33 -> cam sub-common 1;
+ * both sub-commons -> cam-vcore
  * sub-common -> smi-common -> M4U. Every CAMSV
  * engine is its own media device ("mtk-camsv") with one video node, one
  * seninf CSI port sub-device and one sensor (plus its lens); the libcamera
@@ -43,6 +47,20 @@
  * only when its sensor (and VCM) driver is bound, so the modules can load in
  * any order (udev loads them all at boot).
  *
+ * ISP path: CSI port 2 (IMX766) has a second destination, RAW-A, next to
+ * camsv1, so its seninf sub-device has three pads. RAW-A works with RAW-B
+ * as its second engine (mediatek,twin) and each RAW engine with its YUV
+ * engine (mediatek,yuv, in mt6878.dtsi); writers on larbs 16/17 (side A)
+ * and 33/34 (side B). The RAW video node (mtk-camraw driver) is a media
+ * device of its own, outside the CAMSV graph; the sensor and the CSI port
+ * are set up through the camsv1 media device. Nothing of this path is
+ * powered at idle: the RAW engine takes its domain (CAM_SUBA, CAM_SUBB for
+ * side B) and clocks by runtime PM only while its node streams, its YUV
+ * engine and the larbs follow by device links. The driver loads the
+ * request files /lib/firmware/titan2/camraw-start.bin and camraw-frame.bin
+ * when its node is opened; without them the RAW node cannot stream and the
+ * CAMSV path is unchanged.
+ *
  * The S5KGD1SP needs its sensor firmware patch, /lib/firmware/s5kgd1sp_tnp.bin,
  * at stream start. The file is not distributed; the user has to supply it
  * (format: drivers/media/i2c/s5kgd1sp.c).
@@ -168,6 +186,23 @@ &larb29 {
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+/* ISP path: RAW-A (16) and YUV-A (17), RAW-B (33) and YUV-B (34) */
+&larb16 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&larb17 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&larb33 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&larb34 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &m4u {
 	status = "okay";
 };
@@ -453,6 +488,7 @@ imx766_out: endpoint {
 
 /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
 /* seninf: CSI ports 0..2 in, outputs 0..2 to camsv5, camsv2, camsv1    */
+/* (output 2 also to RAW-A)                                             */
 
 &seninf {
 	status = "okay";
@@ -500,9 +536,17 @@ seninf_csi1_out: endpoint {
 };
 
 &seninf_port5 {
+	#address-cells = <1>;
+	#size-cells = <0>;
+
 	seninf_csi2_out: endpoint {
 		remote-endpoint = <&camsv1_in>;
 	};
+
+	seninf_csi2_raw: endpoint@1 {
+		reg = <1>;
+		remote-endpoint = <&cam_raw_a_in>;
+	};
 };
 
 /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
@@ -537,3 +581,30 @@ camsv5_in: endpoint {
 		};
 	};
 };
+
+/* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
+/* ISP path: RAW and YUV engines of both sides (iommus in mt6878.dtsi) */
+
+&cam_raw_a {
+	status = "okay";
+	mediatek,twin = <&cam_raw_b>;
+
+	port {
+		cam_raw_a_in: endpoint {
+			remote-endpoint = <&seninf_csi2_raw>;
+		};
+	};
+};
+
+&cam_yuv_a {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+/* second engine of RAW-A: no input of its own */
+&cam_raw_b {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&cam_yuv_b {
+	status = "okay";
+};
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6878-unihertz-titan2-raw.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6878-unihertz-titan2-raw.dts
index 9c575e3cdef5..4ce4de6d9020 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6878-unihertz-titan2-raw.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6878-unihertz-titan2-raw.dts
@@ -1,70 +1,13 @@
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0-only OR MIT)
 /*
  * Titan 2: TEST board, -all plus the RAW and YUV engines of the image
- * signal processor for the replay of captured command queues
- * (the mtk-camraw-mt6878 driver): larbs 16/17 (side A) and 33/34 (side B) behind
- * the M4U, the engine nodes of both sides with RAW-B as the second engine
- * of RAW-A, and a second destination of CSI port 2 (the main IMX766
- * camera) toward RAW-A next to its CAMSV engine.
+ * signal processor (the mtk-camraw-mt6878 driver) with the second
+ * destination of CSI port 2 (the main IMX766 camera) toward RAW-A.
  *
- * The CSI port of the main camera has three pads on this board; its media
- * device is otherwise the one of -all, and the sensor mode is set there.
- * The RAW video node is outside the media graph. Nothing is powered or
- * written until that node streams, and it needs the request dumps
- * /lib/firmware/titan2/camraw-start.bin and camraw-frame.bin. Side B is
- * powered only with the module parameter twin=1.
- *
- * Boot it as a one-shot entry, -all afterwards.
+ * The -all board now carries that path itself
+ * (mt6878-unihertz-titan2-cameras.dtsi), so this board is the same as
+ * -all. It stays for the boot scripts and may be removed later.
  *
  * Copyright (c) 2026 serlk <22211586+Serlk@users.noreply.github.com>
  */
 #include "mt6878-unihertz-titan2-all.dts"
